     "id": "e1",
     "set": {
      "hidden": false
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "caption": "d1 needs a successor too: d2. Transitivity adds d0 R d2 behind the scenes.",
   "patches": [
    {
     "id": "n2",
     "set": {
      "hidden": false
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "e2",
     "set": {
      "hidden": false
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "caption": "And d3. Every new element is related to all the earlier ones.",
   "patches": [
    {
     "id": "n3",
     "set": {
      "hidden": false
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "e3",
     "set": {
      "hidden": false
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "caption": "Try to stop: let d3's successor be an old element, d0. That closes a cycle d0 R d1 R d2 R d3 R d0.",
   "patches": [
    {
     "id": "back",
     "set": {
      "hidden": false
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "v",
     "set": {
      "text": "d3 R d0 would close a cycle…",
      "tone": "warning"
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "caption": "Transitivity around the cycle gives d0 R d0, which irreflexivity forbids. So no old element can be a successor.",
   "patches": [
    {
     "id": "n0",
     "set": {
      "tone": "danger"
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "v",
     "set": {
      "text": "…but then d0 R d0: forbidden",
      "tone": "danger"
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "caption": "So the chain must keep growing with new elements: no finite model exists. (ℕ, <) is a model: 0 < 1 < 2 < … forever.",
